koserver for Debian
====================

This package installs the koserver binary, a systemd unit, and a
dedicated unprivileged "koserver" system user (created declaratively via
systemd-sysusers) with its state directory /var/lib/koserver (created via
systemd-tmpfiles). Nothing is started automatically on install, since the
defaults probably need a look first:

  1. Edit /etc/koserver/koserver.env (BASE_URL at minimum; it's a
     conffile, so dpkg won't clobber your edits on upgrade).
  2. systemctl enable --now koserver
  3. journalctl -u koserver -f

See /usr/share/doc/koserver/README.md for the full configuration
reference, the KOReader-side setup, and password-recovery options.

`apt remove koserver` keeps both your config (/etc/koserver/koserver.env)
and your data (/var/lib/koserver, the SQLite database). `apt purge
koserver` additionally deletes the config, as usual for a dpkg conffile —
but it still leaves /var/lib/koserver and the "koserver" system user
alone, so a purge can never silently destroy your reading-progress
database; remove those two by hand if you actually want a clean slate.
